# Code Quality & Minimalism

- Keep implementations simple; avoid unnecessary abstraction and premature optimization.
- Avoid unnecessary component fragmentation; split only when it clearly improves maintainability.
- Avoid duplicate code where practical.
- Do not refactor unrelated files or rewrite working code without need.
- Do not introduce libraries for tasks solvable with native HTML/CSS/JS.
- Keep changes focused on the requested task only.
